From 0b5994a3a347c030cd51e1aa314ed918d4f55ff7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 11:28:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gen-loc-config: delete baked-in ethernet on LAN bridge
 members

Before this change, the cidata generated by gen-loc-config emitted only
`set interfaces bridge br0 member interface <iface>` for each LAN
member. The stock small-vyos-ssh-nat.qcow2 base image ships with an
already-declared `interfaces ethernet eth0 { address "dhcp"; hw-id ...;
mtu ...; offload {...} }`, so the resulting candidate config had eth0
both as a bridge member and with a DHCP address. VyOS's
verify_address (configverify.py:227) rejects this combination at
commit time:

  Cannot assign address to interface "eth0" as it is a member of
  bridge "br0"!

vyos-boot-config-loader.py only surfaces this as the generic
`vyos-config[...]: Configuration error` line in syslog because the real
traceback is gated on `vyos-config-debug` in the kernel cmdline.

Emit a `delete interfaces ethernet <iface>` for every LAN bridge
member before any of the bridge `set` lines, wiping the baked-in
address/hw-id/mtu/offload nodes that would otherwise conflict. Delete
on a non-existent path is a non-fatal warning in VyOS, so this is safe
even if a future image stops shipping the offending node.

Also corrected the comment block that previously blamed hw-id for the
commit failure: the prior change which dropped cidata-side hw-id
directives was correct in spirit (no value in adding hw-id on top of
EnforceNetworkInterfaceOrder + net.ifnames=0), but the rationale in
the comment was misattributed.

Verified by rebuilding pkg/pillar, regenerating the live image, and
booting EVE three times (including one boot with a freshly reseeded
VyOS volume): VyOS reaches RUNNING, br0=192.168.33.1/24, admin user
logs in, and no Configuration error appears in /persist/newlog.

Refs olg debug task #27.

Signed-off-by: Mateusz Bajorski <mbajorski@shasta.cloud>
---
 pkg/pillar/cmd/gen-loc-config/main.go | 22 +++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pkg/pillar/cmd/gen-loc-config/main.go b/pkg/pillar/cmd/gen-loc-config/main.go
index 5bd911dec..6cdaceeac 100644
--- a/pkg/pillar/cmd/gen-loc-config/main.go
+++ b/pkg/pillar/cmd/gen-loc-config/main.go
@@ -146,11 +146,9 @@ func generateVyOSUserData(vyosCfg *VyOSConfig) string {
 	//      bus slot per VifOrder — same VM config → same slots every boot.
 	//   2. VyOS's kernel cmdline carries `net.ifnames=0 biosdevname=0`,
 	//      so the kernel uses legacy ethN names assigned by PCI bus order.
-	// We previously emitted `set interfaces ethernet <iface> hw-id '<mac>'`
-	// here as belt-and-suspenders, but VyOS rejects it on bridge members
-	// at commit time ("Cannot assign address to interface as it is a
-	// member of bridge"), which broke first-boot cidata apply. Dropping
-	// hw-id everywhere removes the conflict and the cidata commits cleanly.
+	// No `set interfaces ethernet <iface> hw-id '<mac>'` is emitted — the
+	// pin above is enough, and adding hw-id added nothing useful while
+	// risking drift if the VM gets re-MAC'd.
 
 	// WAN interface: DHCP client
 	add("set interfaces ethernet " + v.WAN + " description 'WAN'")
@@ -165,6 +163,20 @@ func generateVyOSUserData(vyosCfg *VyOSConfig) string {
 		bridgeIP := fmt.Sprintf("%s/%d", v.LANGateway, prefix)
 		networkAddr := ipNet.String()
 
+		// Wipe any baked-in ethernet config on each LAN member before
+		// making it a bridge port. The stock small-vyos-ssh-nat image
+		// ships with `interfaces ethernet eth0 { address "dhcp"; hw-id …;
+		// mtu …; offload {…} }`, and VyOS's verify_address rejects a
+		// bridge member that still has an address — the boot-time commit
+		// fails with `Cannot assign address to interface "eth0" as it is
+		// a member of bridge "br0"!` and load_bootfile then prints the
+		// generic `vyos-config[…]: Configuration error`.
+		// `delete` on a path that does not exist is a non-fatal warning,
+		// so this is safe even if a future image stops shipping the node.
+		for _, iface := range v.LAN {
+			add("delete interfaces ethernet " + iface)
+		}
+
 		// LAN bridge
 		add("set interfaces bridge br0 description 'LAN'")
 		add("set interfaces bridge br0 address '" + bridgeIP + "'")
-- 
2.51.0

